    "q-319490": {
      "dom_id": "step-q319490",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=5+12\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226152/assets/c94a6f3da0e2feb5421ad8652da0dde170d914ea4404a70c37a4112293fe810e.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $0<\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=arctan\\,(\\frac{12}{5})≈1.18,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
