    "q-319581": {
      "dom_id": "step-q319581",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find, **in radians**, the **exact value** of the argument of $z=8\\sqrt{3}-8\\text{i}.$\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226152/assets/78399e67e0ba69c1d7848a41aa5d4a5f8040fc578aab30a99f7e19ac86ece179.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{8\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
